{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"99 cents only\" because closing)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_172195389#3_376092682","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3548","rank":1,"snippet":"struggling There are a handful of discount retailers in the US, including Dollar General, <cover>99 Cents Only, and Five Below. But while fellow off-price retail stores like T.J. Maxx and Marshall’s thrive on a chaotic environment, where stores are jam-packed with a sometimes disorganized array of discounted products, shoppers have pointed out that Dollar Tree and Family Dollar are often disappointing destinations. The chains are plagued with empty shelves and messy stores. Dollar stores have long been considered by retail analysts as able to compete with big box brands because of their additional discounts and their often-smaller stores. In the past few years, though, Walmart has been experimenting with smaller-store concepts. Walmart has also been aggressively trying to squeeze out its dollar-store competitors by lowering the costs of items like detergent and cereal. A Dollar Tree store in Miami on July 28, 2014. Joe Raedle/Getty Images Amazon, too, has had its eye on the dollar store space.\" , \"start_char\": 1907.000000 , \"title\": \"Dollar Tree is closing </cover>almost 400 Family Dollar stores this year - Vox\" , \"url\":"}}
